@page "/demo/tabs-accordion"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared

@* 2026-10-12: new page on FeatureDemoLayout; three examples (tab control, tab strip, accordion). Facts checked against Navigation/TabControl.razor,
   Navigation/TabItem.razor, TabStripControl.razor, TabStripModels.cs, AccordionControl.razor, AccordionItemControl.razor and their stylesheets
   (FlexCore 0.2.50). The accordion moved here from UI elements. *@

@* 2026-10-26 (review comment: "more like tabs, with an outline and an x to close, in FlexCore style"): both tab examples sit
   in a .folder-tabs wrapper whose page CSS draws outlined folder tabs (gray resting tabs, a white active tab joined to its pane by a
   blue top edge); the CSS tab shows it. TabControl has no close button, so the closable tabs are the tab strip's, now laid out like
   a document workspace: a pinned Home tab and closable documents. Sample data moved from a kitchen estimate to the site's travel
   theme. *@

@* 2026-10-28: FlexCore 0.2.49+ gave TabStripControl (and TabControl through it) Theme, Orientation, a right-click menu for both,
   overflow navigation and separators. The page CSS that drew folder tabs is gone: both examples use TabTheme.FolderTabs, the
   document tabs example switches theme with a button group and orientation with the strip's own menu, and the doc tables carry
   the new members (checked against TabStripControl.razor, TabStripModels.cs, TabStripControl.razor.css, Navigation/TabControl.razor). *@

@* 2026-10-29: the tab control example takes the site's tab style (the top menu's look, as on every code tab and the chart
   gallery): Minimal theme, one Horizontal row and the site-tabs class from app.css, whose rules the CSS tab prints through
   AppSource.Region. The document tabs keep the library themes, since their buttons switch them and site-tabs would override all five. *@

@* 2026-11-14: the tab control example shows the library's own themes and layouts again (buttons bound with @bind-Theme and
   @bind-Orientation, one tab through Content) and no longer takes the site-tabs class, which hid all five themes. Its CSS tab
   prints the page's own rules. The accessibility notes and the CSS classes row are corrected against TabStripControl.razor. *@

<PageTitle>Blazor Tabs, TabStrip and Accordion — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Tabs & accordion" Category="Components" ControlName="TabControl · TabStripControl · AccordionControl"
                   Tagline="Show one section at a time with tabs, document tabs or an accordion."
                   SourcePath="Navigation/TabControl.razor; TabStripControl.razor; AccordionControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>TabControl</code> is a Blazor tab control: users switch between sections of a page, and only the selected pane renders. Use <code>TabStripControl</code> for document tabs users close, with the content kept elsewhere, and <code>AccordionControl</code> for stacked sections that expand in place, as on a narrow settings page. Both tab controls come in five themes and let users change orientation from a right-click menu.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="tabs" Title="Tab control" RazorCode="@Code.Tabs" CSharpCode="@Code.TabsCs" CssCode="@Code.TabsCss">
            <Description><p>Switch between the Summary, Lines and Notes of a trip quote; only the selected pane renders. Pick a theme and a layout with the buttons, or right-click the tabs: every tab control carries that menu, and <code>&#64;bind-Theme</code> and <code>&#64;bind-Orientation</code> follow it.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonGroupControl Items="_themeItems" Values="@(new[] { _tabTheme.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="SetTabTheme" Selection="ChoiceSelectionMode.Single" AriaLabel="Tab theme" />
                <ButtonGroupControl Items="_layoutItems" Values="@(new[] { _tabLayout.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="SetTabLayout" Selection="ChoiceSelectionMode.Single" AriaLabel="Tab layout" />
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <div class="quote-tabs">
                    <TabControl @bind-SelectedIndex="_tab" @bind-Theme="_tabTheme" @bind-Orientation="_tabLayout">
                        <TabItems>
                            <TabItem HeaderText="Summary">
                                <dl class="summary">
                                    <dt>Request</dt><dd>LIS-0001 Lisbon city break</dd>
                                    <dt>Status</dt><dd>Quoted, 3 lines</dd>
                                    <dt>Total</dt><dd>$1,720</dd>
                                </dl>
                            </TabItem>
                            <TabItem HeaderText="Lines">
                                <table class="lines">
                                    <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Qty</th><th class="num">Amount</th></tr></thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr><td>Return flights</td><td>2 seats</td><td class="num">$420</td></tr>
                                        <tr><td>Old-town hotel</td><td>4 nights</td><td class="num">$1,120</td></tr>
                                        <tr><td>Guided food tour</td><td>2 people</td><td class="num">$180</td></tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </TabItem>
                            <TabItem HeaderText="Notes">
                                <Content>
                                    <p class="m0">Quote valid 14 days. The travelers prefer a morning flight; the hotel holds the rooms until Friday.</p>
                                </Content>
                            </TabItem>
                        </TabItems>
                    </TabControl>
                </div>
                <p class="result">Tab @(_tab + 1) of 3 selected · @_tabTheme, @_tabLayout</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="strip" Title="Document tabs" RazorCode="@Code.Strip" CSharpCode="@Code.StripCs" CssCode="@Code.StripCss">
            <Description><p>Close a document with its ×, pick a theme with the buttons, and right-click the strip to change its orientation.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonGroupControl Items="_themeItems" Values="@(new[] { _theme.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="SetTheme" Selection="ChoiceSelectionMode.Single" AriaLabel="Tab theme" />
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <div class="@(_orientation == TabOrientation.Vertical ? "docs docs-vertical" : "docs")">
                    <TabStripControl Items="_docs" @bind-SelectedIndex="_doc" OnTabClose="CloseDoc" @bind-Theme="_theme" @bind-Orientation="_orientation" AriaLabel="Documents" />
                    <div class="strip-pane">@(_docs.Count == 0 ? "No documents open." : _docs[Math.Clamp(_doc, 0, _docs.Count - 1)].Tag)</div>
                </div>
                <div class="strip-actions">
                    <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="Reopen" Disabled="@(_closed.Count == 0)">Reopen last closed</ButtonControl>
                    <span class="result">@_docs.Count open, @_closed.Count closed · @_theme, @_orientation</span>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="accordion" Title="Accordion" RazorCode="@Code.Accordion">
            <Description><p>Open several sections; without <code>Multiple</code>, opening one closes the rest.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="acc">
                    <AccordionControl Multiple="true">
                        <AccordionItemControl Title="Traveler" IconCss="bi bi-person" InitiallyExpanded="true">Clementine Marmalade, two adults, repeat client.</AccordionItemControl>
                        <AccordionItemControl Title="Flights" IconCss="bi bi-airplane">Return to Lisbon, morning departure, one checked bag each.</AccordionItemControl>
                        <AccordionItemControl Title="Notes" IconCss="bi bi-sticky">Quote valid 14 days.</AccordionItemControl>
                        <AccordionItemControl Title="Attachments (none)" IconCss="bi bi-paperclip" Disabled="true">—</AccordionItemControl>
                    </AccordionControl>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-tabcontrol-parameters" Title="TabControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TabControl.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TabControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.TabControl" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-tabitem-parameters" Title="TabItem parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TabItem.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TabItem parameters" Rows="Vocab.TabItem" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-tabstripcontrol-parameters" Title="TabStripControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Strip.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TabStripControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Strip" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-tabstripitem" Title="TabStripItem" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.StripItem.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="TabStripItem" Rows="Vocab.StripItem" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-accordioncontrol-parameters" Title="AccordionControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Accordion.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="AccordionControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Accordion" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-accordionitemcontrol-parameters" Title="AccordionItemControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.AccordionItem.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="AccordionItemControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.AccordionItem" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-variables-tabstripcontrol-only" Title="CSS variables (TabStripControl only)" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Vars.Length, "variables")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssVariables" Title="CSS variables (TabStripControl only)" Rows="Vocab.Vars" />
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li><code>TabControl</code> draws its headers with a <code>TabStripControl</code>, so both have the same keyboard: the headers are a <code>tablist</code> of <code>role="tab"</code> elements with <code>aria-selected</code>, and the selected one is the single Tab stop.</li>
            <li>On a tab, Left or Up selects the previous enabled tab and Right or Down the next; Home and End select the first and last; Delete closes a closable tab. Focus follows the selection.</li>
            <li>The tab control's pane is a plain <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>: it is not a <code>tabpanel</code> and is not linked to its tab. Every tab control's list is named "Tabs"; a strip used directly takes its name from <code>AriaLabel</code>.</li>
            <li>Each accordion header is a button with <code>aria-expanded</code>; the body is a <code>role="region"</code>. A disabled header is a disabled button.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Dockable tab groups the user can split and float: <a href="demo/dock-manager">Dock manager</a>. Keyboard focus order across the controls of a page: <a href="demo/page-navigation">Page navigation</a>.</li>
            <li>Side-by-side and collapsible regions: <a href="demo/layout">Page layouts</a>. A navigation tree: <a href="demo/tree/treeview-explorer">Tree view</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

